Honest deviations from GPT's literal numbers (implementation-level only,
design unchanged):
- Confetti pieces are 12x28 px with a 4 px outline instead of the
  specified 14 px outline: a 14 px stroke on a 12 px-wide piece would
  cover the fill completely, leaving solid black bars instead of the
  specified green/gold/red confetti.
- Trophy handles are smooth curves through GPT's specified points
  (GPT's own description says "curved handle"); the endpoints are GPT's.
- In the Champion pose the antenna bead and cap button are hidden behind
  the trophy (GPT's fix2 states this explicitly); the cap wings, the
  face and the newspaper torso stay visible.
- In the At Work pose the gold seal and most of the newspaper fold are
  hidden behind the monitor (the monitor sits in front of the torso, per
  spec); the headline stays fully visible.
- In the At Work pose there is a 10 px gap between the monitor bottom
  (y=780) and the desk top (y=790); the keyboard (y=764-794) covers the
  middle of it, so it reads as a thin shadow line.
- In the Champion pose the raised forearms pass just inside the face
  screen's left/right edges and clip a few px of the outer eye corners;
  the eyes and smile remain clearly readable.

